abstract: >-
  SATROOT is an Apache-2.0 protocol and dependency-free pure-Python
  reference implementation for deterministic, replayable semantic
  ledgers. A ledger is an append-only log of canonically serialized,
  signed events; anyone holding the log and the public keys can
  recompute the exact state and its hash offline, with no server and no
  trust in the operator. Typed object profiles (stable reference units,
  machine credits, receipts, identities, licenses, and event-stream
  custody) sit above a frozen kernel, alongside a publication ladder of
  signed bundles, releases, catalogs, and registries. Ledger state
  hashes can optionally be committed on-chain in OP_RETURN envelopes
  and verified from raw transaction bytes.
